  "headline": "Government Proposes 50% Seat Hike and Women’s Quota in New Bill",
  "seoTitle": "Union Cabinet Tables Amended Delimitation Bill",
  "metaDescription": "The Indian government plans to introduce the Delimitation (Second) Bill, 2026, proposing a 50% seat increase and a one-third women's reservation quota.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "The proposed Delimitation (Second) Bill, 2026, aims to increase parliamentary and state assembly seats by 50%.",
    "New provisions include a one-third reservation quota for women in the Lok Sabha and state assemblies.",
    "The legislation utilizes 1971 census data for seat counts while applying 2011 census data for boundary determinations."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indian government is set to introduce the revised Delimitation (Second) Bill, 2026, during an upcoming special session of Parliament. This legislation replaces a previous version and includes significant structural changes, most notably a proposed 50 percent increase in the number of parliamentary and state assembly seats. Additionally, the proposal incorporates the Constitution 132nd Amendment Bill, 2026, which mandates a one-third reservation for women in legislative bodies. Discussions regarding the bill have sparked political debate, with tensions surfacing over the voting eligibility of certain members amid ongoing defection disputes and questions from parties like the DMK regarding the fairness of the delimitation exercise. The Delimitation Commission intends to use 1971 census data to determine seat totals while utilizing 2011 data to define constituency boundaries, aiming to address demographic growth while maintaining legislative balance.",
